# hw definition for a MatekF405-Wing-bdshot variant with the "LED" pad back as
# PWM output 10, as in upstream ArduPilot.
#
# The fork's MatekF405-Wing hwdef turns the LED pad (PA15) into a RELAY_1
# GPIO, which leaves 9 outputs. This variant restores upstream's
# PA15 TIM2_CH1 PWM(10). TIM2 drives nothing else on this board (system timer
# is TIM5, RC input TIM9), so output 10 is its own group and can run a
# different PWM rate from 1-9.
#
# NODMA: TIM2_UP's only DMA stream (DMA1 stream 1) is USART3_RX's, which the
# bdshot base keeps free for full-DMA UART3 (use it for the RC receiver). So
# output 10 is PWM only - no DShot on it.
#
# Cost: relay 1 no longer has a default pin (RELAY1_PIN -1). Point RELAY1_PIN
# at a spare output's GPIO (50-59, with that SERVOn_FUNCTION -1) to keep one.
#
# Name is not MatekF405-Wing-bdshot-LED because board names are capped at
# 23 characters. Board ID is inherited, so the .apj flashes over the stock
# bootloader as a normal firmware update.

include ../MatekF405-Wing-bdshot/hwdef.dat

undef PA15 RELAY1_PIN_DEFAULT
PA15 TIM2_CH1 TIM2 PWM(10) GPIO(59) NODMA
